[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873286118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116105#issuecomment-3873286118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116105","id":3873286118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m3afm","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T18:33:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T18:34:52Z","body":"> Performance impact should be negligible\r\n\r\nFor what it's worth, `_encode_string` is doing this already:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/377b5a31752ad5e9c53733639ba0d263e1158645/core/io/marshalls.cpp#L1316-L1321\r\n\r\n> Though in most cases, the buffer would have contained 0s anyway (by chance).\r\n\r\nI guess that might depend on the platform's allocator, and what you mean by most cases, but on Linux (Fedora 43) I have a fairly high repro rate. With just 3 `NodePath` instances in a `*.gdc` file (from using `NodePath` literals) I had an almost 100% non-deterministic export output of said file.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873286118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873362184","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116105#issuecomment-3873362184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116105","id":3873362184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m3tEI","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T18:49:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T18:49:39Z","body":"I've read somewhere that most OSs wipe pages of RAM to 0 before handing them out to applications, for security reasons. Which would mean you only get non-0 allocations if your allocator is re-allocating previously acquired memory. From my testing, that was very rare (though admittedly i tested fresh process instances out of convenience, so fresh allocations would have been expected).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/38